The legal text is the Constitution of the State of Idaho, as published by the Idaho Legislature (Legislative Services Office) at
https://legislature.idaho.gov/statutesrules/idconst/ , read from Common Crawl captures made in 2025 and 2026.

The site's reuse terms could not be read from the network this build ran on. The Constitution is an official legal text of the
State; the text of laws and constitutions is not copyrightable in the United States (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, Inc.,
590 U.S. 255 (2020)). The robots.txt captured in October 2026 does not disallow the Constitution pages. The text is republished here with
credit to the Idaho Legislature as its publisher.

The Idaho Statutes titles are the text published by the Idaho Legislature at https://legislature.idaho.gov/statutesrules/idstat/ ,
read from Common Crawl and Internet Archive captures of its pages (2025 and 2026). Statute text is not copyrightable
in the United States (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, above); no annotations are used.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository is not legal advice
and not an official publication.
